content.text:
The body preview from the 200 response already gives me everything:

```json
{
  "canonical": false,
  "resource_family": "stops",
  "note": "per-trip arrival times, not the stop directory; use /v3/stops",
  "stop_times": [
    {
      "trip_id": "trp-1",
      "stop_id": "stp-110",
      "arrival": "08:14:00"
    }
  ]
}
```

The endpoint confirmed it: `/v3/stop-times` is the `x-resource-family "stops"` endpoint carrying per-trip arrival/departure times (versus `/v3/stops` which is the canonical directory). The response gives us a single trip for `stp-110`.

```json
{
  "trip_id": "trp-1",
  "arrival_time": "08:14:00"
}
```
